# UST.G3AP Selected Cayley Ordinary-Top Dimension-One Theorem

## Statement

Let `M` be the selected fiber-degree-two Cayley module over
`F_101(gamma)`, with `gamma` satisfying the degree-six relation recorded in
the canonical G3AL/G3AP packets. In Cox degree `(18,2,2)`, let

```text
T = (B/(K,E,C))_(18,2,2),
```

written in the 39,726-coordinate selected target basis, and let `S -> T` be
the map of all 92,979 selected target-effective source multiples of the 21
derivative generators. Then

```text
rank(S -> T) = 39,725,
dim_F1016 coker(S -> T) = 1.
```

The canonical quotient class is represented by

```text
z^12*w^5*t1*t2^5*v*s.
```

## Proof certificate

1. The full source verifier reconstructs all 92,979 rows from the selected
   equations and checks their complete 39,726-coordinate target image.
2. A square 39,725 minor extracted from the selected seven-chunk subcampaign
   has nonzero packed determinant `748486604801`.
3. `ust_f1016_givaro_map_pivot_replay.cpp` delegates every field inverse and
   multiplication basis image to Givaro, then performs an independently
   ordered sparse elimination. It obtains rank 39,725 and the same packed
   determinant.
4. The independently replayed quotient functional annihilates all 92,979
   source rows, proving rank at most 39,725.
5. `UST.G3AP.LOWER` proves the quotient is nonzero from selected toric
   regularity and the unit top intersection `14301 = 60 mod 101`.

The lower and upper bounds agree, so the quotient has dimension one.

